        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "5677695e-1bf7-5785-8a06-950c80c280d6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Matthew O'Neill, Jon Alpert, Dorothy Parker, Robert Benchley, George S. Kaufman, Edna Ferber, Marc Connelly, Harold Ross, Harpo Marx\n- Products: Baghdad ER, The Ten-Year Lunch: The Wit and Legend of the Algonquin Round Table, Redemption\n- Organizations: HBO\n- Concepts: Algonquin Round Table\n- Places: New York City\n\nFacts:\n- The Ten-Year Lunch: The Wit and Legend of the Algonquin Round Table is a 1987 American documentary film about the Algonquin Round Table in New York City.\n- The Algonquin Round Table was a floating group of writers and actors in the Roaring Twenties that included Dorothy Parker, Robert Benchley, George S. Kaufman, Edna Ferber, Marc Connelly, Harold Ross, and Harpo Marx.\n- Baghdad ER is a documentary released by HBO on May 21, 2006.\n- Matthew O'Neill is a documentary filmmaker best known for his work on the HBO film Baghdad ER.\n- Matthew O'Neill and Jon Alpert won three Emmy Awards for Baghdad ER.\n- Redemption is a 2012 short documentary film directed by Jon Alpert and Matthew O'Neill.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
